ment:\n\n$$\n¬(A∨¬B){{field-4}}¬A∧B\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $B≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬A∧B & ≡¬\\text{T}∧\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∧\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $B≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬A∧B & ≡¬\\text{T}∧\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∧\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{F}$ and $B≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(A∨¬B) & ≡¬(\\text{F}∨¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡¬(\\text{F}∨\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∨¬B)\\,$ | $\\,¬A∧B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\n \n\nTo determine whether $¬(A∨¬B)$ is logically equivalent to $¬A∧B,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\text{F},\\text{F},\\text{T},\\text{F}).$ Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n¬(A∨¬B)≡¬A∧B.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376361 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a6a36e8-e14e-5051-acae-48de63ff3eff" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalent Statements Using Partially Completed Truth Tables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f25a409-c3df-5f29-8780-55d89ecc8c01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376363} {:answer/id #uuid "687a2c9a-680d-54ad-82d1-6a7336b5cb57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376364}] 