{F}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P≡\\text{F}$ and $Q≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬P∨Q & ≡¬\\text{F}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below. \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,Q∨¬(P∨Q)\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $Q∨¬(P∨Q)$ is logically equivalent to $¬P∨Q,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\text{T},\\text{F},\\text{T},\\text{T}).$ Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\nQ∨¬(P∨Q)≡¬P∨Q.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc5b8688-3838-5e9e-9304-9a4c787034ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ca8340a-82df-55a3-9305-a651afdc38de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471663} {:answer/id #uuid "b512a5e7-a7fe-581c-9548-feb54ed21083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ca8340a-82df-55a3-9305-a651afdc38de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471663} :answer-field/id #uuid "22724fc6-7046-54cf-a41e-738bcd859a57" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472337} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "329d9332-b